  "research": {
    "area-3": {
      "text": "Why scout here\n\nThis area around Don Mills Road and Lawrence Avenue East in Toronto presents a strong commercial environment, particularly with the presence of CF Shops at Don Mills, a large lifestyle center with numerous retail and dining options.\n\nThe \"Shops at Don Mills\" area is described as a \"true centrepiece of the community\" with both residential and retail spaces, indicating a potentially steady local customer base.\n\nNearby concepts and menu checks\n\nThe Shops at Don Mills features a variety of dining options, including Eataly, which opened a location there in late May, and other restaurants such as Scaddabush Italian Kitchen, Joey Don Mills Grill/Lounge, and Jack Astor's Bar & Grill.\n\nThere are also cafes like Pablo's Coffee House and The Purple Bakeshop within the center.\n\nNear the Aga Khan Museum, which is a short distance away, options include Diwan (which has a courtyard café) and various restaurants in nearby plazas like Asian Legend and Kitaya Japanese Takeout.\n\nAccess and local context\n\nThe area is well-connected, situated at Don Mills Road and Lawrence Avenue East, with good proximity to the Don Valley Parkway (DVP).\n\nOn-site parking is available at Shops at Don Mills, including surface lots and a multi-level parkade.\n\nPublic transit routes also serve the location.\n\nThe Shops at Don Mills is described as a \"lifestyle centre\" with storefronts facing a network of private internal streets, creating a pedestrian-friendly environment.",
